-- Kept on ASSUME deliberately (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.1, R0: ASSUME is deprecated): TYPICALLY on a type ASSUME is an error the opaque DECLARE spelling has no analogue for.
-- TYPICALLY defaults are meaningless on a TYPE binder (a type variable or a
-- TYPE assumption): a "default value" for a type makes no sense, so it is
-- rejected rather than silently dropped.

-- ERROR: TYPICALLY on a TYPE assumption
ASSUME `some type` IS A TYPE TYPICALLY 42

-- ERROR: TYPICALLY on a TYPE parameter
GIVEN a IS A TYPE TYPICALLY 42
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bad type param` IF TRUE
